{{ ansible_managed | comment }}
# openbao-node-converge — the workstation-held converge identity for the
# OpenBao-node play (`--tags openbao` on `openbao_group`), which is the single
# converge this estate still runs from a workstation rather than the execution
# plane, because its inputs are the seal key and the provisioning identities
# (docs/agents/commands-and-testing.md).
#
# It exists so that play does not need `ansible-converge`. That identity is the
# estate-wide consumer inventory and also serves every plane-triggered
# production converge; adding a workstation source range to it would widen the
# blast radius of the broadest converge credential there is, to fix one play.
# This role is instead a strict SUBSET of it — every path below appears
# verbatim in ansible-converge-policy.hcl.j2 — bound to the workstation CIDR
# class and inert (no standing secret_id).
#
# WHAT THE PLAY ACTUALLY TOUCHES, and therefore all this grants:
#
#   platform/object-storage
#     The shared `inventory_resolve` role fetches the tofu-published inventory
#     artifact from object storage. Call site: inventory/load_tofu.yml. Without
#     it the play matches no hosts at all.
#
#   platform/ansible/env (both mounts)
#     The run environment: the env-lookup values roles/openbao asserts on
#     before it writes anything — the AppRole CIDR classes
#     (08-admin-and-ttls.yml), the SSH CA source-address list
#     (05-ssh-ca-engine.yml), the host-key pin. Empty values here do not fail
#     quietly; they trip the converge's own asserts. Read only — a converge
#     never writes these.
#
# The OpenBao ADMINISTRATIVE work of the play — KV mounts, seeds, policies,
# AppRoles, engines, snapshots — is NOT granted here and must not be. That
# plane authenticates with `openbao_bootstrap_token` (the break-glass
# provisioning token, or openbao-reconcile), never with the converge identity;
# see roles/openbao/tasks/init/02-initialize-cluster.yml. A grant here would
# create a second path to the control plane wearing a converge identity's name.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT GRANTED, all of which ansible-converge does carry:
#   * apps/nas, platform/windows-vdi/win11-admin, platform/defaults — read by
#     roles this play never runs.
#   * ai/mcp/{splunk,vikunja,zammad,nautobot} write — MCP publication belongs
#     to the converges that mint those tokens.
#   * secrets-external/platform/backblaze-splunk — the ansible-splunk converge.
#   * the openbao_credential_publish_apps write loop — this play publishes no
#     app credential.
#   * config-write — the OpenBao play authors no `config` mount content.
# SSH certificate signing is not granted here either: it is the existing
# `ssh-sign-automation-ansible` capability leaf, attached alongside this policy
# in the AppRole declaration rather than restated as a path.

{% for kv_path in ['platform/object-storage'] %}
path "{{ openbao_kv_mount }}/data/{{ kv_path }}" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

path "{{ openbao_kv_mount }}/metadata/{{ kv_path }}" {
  capabilities = ["read", "list"]
}

{% endfor %}
{% for mount in [openbao_kv_mount, 'secrets-external'] %}
path "{{ mount }}/data/platform/ansible/env" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

path "{{ mount }}/metadata/platform/ansible/env" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

{% endfor %}
